# chorus low-latency vector: the stream stream_k3_d2.
#
# Committed, and never written by a test (crates/protocol/examples/lowlat_vectors.rs
# wrote it). Pushing chunk.0 onward through the FEC encoder (fec_k, fec_depth) and
# sealing what it emits with `key` and `stream_tag`, counters from first_counter,
# must give plaintext.N and datagram.N byte for byte, in that order
# (docs/protocol.md, "Low-latency path"). The cases (case_*.fields) drop, reorder,
# repeat and alter these datagrams.
#
# Format: one "key = value" per line, '#' starts a comment; bytes are hex.
#
# Column interleave: k 3, depth 2. Each block of 6 chunks holds two groups, the
# even chunks and the odd ones, so two consecutive losses cost each group one.

